{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/reviews/id1718027183"}, "name":{"label":"iluvbooks413"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2025-06-16T21:40:58-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.6.15.0"}, "id":{"label":"12783633167"}, "title":{"label":"Best game? I think so."}, "content":{"label":"I’m going to be super honest here: I hate farming games. Animal Crossing gets on my nerves after a while. And also? I just never found them entertaining. No plot, no end goal. Yuck.\n\nBut then I played Stardew Valley. And saying that my whole world turned around would be an understatement.\n\nI never had as much fun with a farming game as I have with this. There’s just something about it that is so charming, so alluring that makes me want to play for hours on end.\n\nMaybe it’s the liberation that it provides, allowing you to be and do whatever you want.\n\nMaybe it’s the in-game graphics and pixel drawings of characters (which I will say are beautiful).\n\nOr maybe it’s that Stardew is altogether different from the crowd.\n\nTL;DR:\n\nI usually hate farming games. But this one? I could grind for hours and hours and STILL have my sanity 😅!\n\nSo, looking to try something new? Stardew Valley is waiting. Pay the five bucks for hours of endless entertainment.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/us/review?id=1406710800&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
